SN MegaWho v1.1

This tiny utility does a continuous WHO scan until a key is pressed.  The
ANSI version works alot better, but non-ANSI is supported and they both
do the same thing for the most part.

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)

 2  Place "MWHO" in your SysText:Help/ directory.

 3  Edit the SN_MegaWho file and change the who command to whatever you
    use.  (I use a different who normally, but it doesn't work well with
    this, so I changed CNet's internal who to oldwho.)

 4  Add "MWHO |{#0<path>SN_MegaWho}" to your bbsmenu under either
    "2; Available everywhere" or "3; Main prompt."  Modify your online
    menu(s)) to reflect the new addition.  Note that the above { is
    actually a control-Q command.

 5  Reload your bbstext/bbsmenu via CNet's Control Panel menu (option
    #3, "Text/menu reload  RAmiga-T" and you're all set!

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

